#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186059479 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "5dbfd5f3-553b-5276-8716-bbceddefc4d3" :knowledge-point/title "Multiplying 2x2 Square Matrices"}] :question/id #uuid "04e1822f-2da1-5b28-8967-7a0026c39319" :question/math-academy-id "e-4401" :question/problem "Find $AB$ and $BA,$ if \n$[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ -5 & 1\\end{aligned}]$\nand\n$[\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 2\\end{aligned}]$" :question/worked-solution "Multiplying each row in the first matrix by each column in the second, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}AB & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ -5 & 1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 2\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}1\\cdot 0+0\\cdot (-1) & 1\\cdot 1+0\\cdot 2 \\\\ -5\\cdot 0+1\\cdot (-1) & -5\\cdot 1+1\\cdot 2\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 \\\\ -1 & -3\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nand\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}BA & =[\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 2\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ -5 & 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}0\\cdot 1+1\\cdot (-5) & 0\\cdot 0+1\\cdot 1 \\\\ -1\\cdot 1+2\\cdot (-5) & -1\\cdot 0+2\\cdot 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-5 & 1 \\\\ -11 & 2\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n**Watch out!** Notice that \n\n$$\nAB \\neq BA.\n$$\n\nMatrix multiplication is not **commutative**, meaning that when we switch the order of multiplication, we often get a different result (like we did in this example)."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186059480 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "9c7a77cf-163a-542a-b4a3-4274344b9cf8" :knowledge-point/title "Multiplying 3x3 Square Matrices"}] :question/id #uuid "3b0c400c-89bd-504d-87c3-e0f24957d42b" :question/math-academy-id "e-4402" :question/problem "Find $AB$, if \n$[\\begin{aligned}-2 & 0 & 3 \\\\ 3 & -1 & -2 \\\\ -2 & 0 & -1\\end{aligned}]$\nand\n$[\\begin{aligned}0 & 3 & -2 \\\\ 1 & -2 & 4 \\\\ -3 & -1 & 2\\end{aligned}]$" :question/worked-solution "Multiplying each row in the first matrix by each column in the second, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}AB & =[\\begin{aligned}-2 & 0 & 3 \\\\ 3 & -1 & -2 \\\\ -2 & 0 & -1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}0 & 3 & -2 \\\\ 1 & -2 & 4 \\\\ -3 & -1 & 2\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}0+0-9 & -6+0-3 & 4+0+6 \\\\ 0-1+6 & 9+2+2 & -6-4-4 \\\\ 0+0+3 & -6+0+1 & 4+0-2\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-9 & -9 & 10 \\\\ 5 & 13 & -14 \\\\ 3 & -5 & 2\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186059523 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "a827b0d0-faa2-521f-b166-e13873b1da00" :knowledge-point/title "Finding an Entry of the Product of Two Matrices"}] :question/id #uuid "4aaa04dd-1380-50c9-8118-52f6e414f830" :question/math-academy-id "e-5255" :question/problem "Let $Z=XY.$ What is the value of $z_{32}$, if\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & 0 \\\\ -2 & 0 & -1 \\\\ 1 & 2 & 3\\end{aligned}]\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Multiplying the $3$rd row in $X$ by the $2$nd column in $Y$, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{z}_{32} & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & 3\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 4 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =1\\cdot (-1)+2\\cdot 4+3\\cdot (-2) \\\\  & =-1+8-6 \\\\  & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186276879 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "9c7a77cf-163a-542a-b4a3-4274344b9cf8" :knowledge-point/title "Multiplying 3x3 Square Matrices"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "b44ba48d-8b90-53e9-bea6-b0ab3599dc53" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}11 & -2 & 7 \\\\ -1 & 3 & 2 \\\\ 10 & -2 & 8\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186276881} {:answer/id #uuid "4bc0abac-0053-5f11-b3cc-876cab2a77cc" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}10 & -2 & 7 \\\\ -1 & 3 & 2 \\\\ 10 & 2 & 8\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186276882} {:answer/id #uuid "9f3abd15-c109-5dc3-a9e1-204ed0e1457f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}11 & -2 & 7 \\\\ 1 & 3 & 2 \\\\ 10 & 2 & 8\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186276883} {:answer/id #uuid "9683f5bd-d49a-5027-9829-3e007d2b8146" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}11 & -2 & 7 \\\\ -1 & 3 & 2 \\\\ 10 & 2 & -8\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186276884} {:answer/id #uuid "6f49ae3b-6693-58a4-8310-c2f2067d6592" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}11 & -2 & 7 \\\\ -1 & 3 & 2 \\\\ 10 & 2 & 8\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186276885}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "6f49ae3b-6693-58a4-8310-c2f2067d6592" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}11 & -2 & 7 \\\\ -1 & 3 & 2 \\\\ 10 & 2 & 8\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186276885} :answer-field/id #uuid "041803c3-f744-5b47-8f26-b4c3e845d80a" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186276880}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "8b7ac6bc-6401-5b81-8e83-9d9f1552f0e7" :question/math-academy-id "q-11568" :question/problem "Find $ST$,  if  $S=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 4 \\\\ 0 & -5 & 2 \\\\ 2 & 0 & 2\\end{aligned}]$ and $T=[\\begin{aligned}3 & 2 & 3 \\\\ 1 & -1 & 0 \\\\ 2 & -1 & 1\\end{aligned}].$" :question/worked-solution "Multiplying each row in the first matrix by each column in the second, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}ST & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 4 \\\\ 0 & -5 & 2 \\\\ 2 & 0 & 2\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}3 & 2 & 3 \\\\ 1 & -1 & 0 \\\\ 2 & -1 & 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}3+0+8 & 2+0-4 & 3+0+4 \\\\ 0-5+4 & 0+5-2 & 0-0+2 \\\\ 6+0+4 & 4-0-2 & 6+0+2\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}11 & -2 & 7 \\\\ -1 & 3 & 2 \\\\ 10 & 2 & 8\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186059921 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/